/**
 * @defgroup StarAgmlUtil StarAgmlUtil — AGML Geometry Utilities
 * @brief Supporting infrastructure for the AGML geometry framework.
 * @ingroup StarAgmlLib
 *
 * `StarAgmlUtil` provides four utilities consumed by `StarAgmlLib` and by
 * geometry module code:
 *
 * - `AgParameterList<T>` — generic typed named-parameter store, used as a
 *   mixin base by `AgShape`, `AgMaterial`, `AgMedium`, `AgAttribute`,
 *   `AgPlacement`, `AgPosition`, and `AgCreate`.
 * - `AgTransform` — 4×4 homogeneous-matrix arithmetic for coordinate
 *   transformations (translations, axis rotations, G3 angle notation, ORT
 *   permutations, matrix multiply, inversion).
 * - `AgMLPosition` — a self-contained position/rotation record combining
 *   `AgTransform` with `AgParameterList<double>` and run-time DB-misalignment
 *   support.
 * - `AgMLDb` / `AgMLDbFunctor` — singleton functor interface through which
 *   misalignment matrices are fetched from the STAR geometry database.
 *
 * @par Related modules
 * - @ref StarAgmlLib  — core AGML geometry description library
 * - @ref StarAgmlChecker — material-budget analysis
 * - @ref StarAgmlViewer  — interactive geometry viewer
 *
 * @{
 */

/**
 * @class AgParameterList
 * @brief Generic typed named-parameter store used throughout the AGML framework.
 * @ingroup StarAgmlUtil
 *
 * `AgParameterList<T>` is a template mixin that provides `par(name)`,
 * `isSet(name)`, `hasPar(name)`, and `unSet(name)` operations over a
 * `std::map<string,T>`.  In addition to the parameter map it carries
 * placement-context strings: block name, mother name, alignment group name,
 * DB table name, chair name, and row number.  These context fields are
 * propagated through the stacker to enable per-placement DB lookups.
 *
 * All concrete AGML parameter-bearing classes (`AgShape`, `AgMaterial`,
 * `AgMedium`, `AgAttribute`, `AgPlacement`, `AgPosition`, `AgCreate`) inherit
 * from `AgParameterList<double>`.
 */

/**
 * @class AgTransform
 * @brief 4×4 homogeneous-matrix arithmetic for coordinate transformations.
 * @ingroup StarAgmlUtil
 *
 * Maintains an internal 4×4 matrix `mMatrix` and exposes the following
 * operations:
 * - `Translate(x,y,z)` / `TranslateX/Y/Z(delta)` — accumulate a translation.
 * - `RotateX/Y/Z(alpha)` — rotate about a coordinate axis (degrees).
 * - `Ortho("+X+Y+Z")` — apply an axis-permutation/sign transformation.
 * - `Angles(θx,φx,θy,φy,θz,φz)` — set rotation from six G3 angles.
 * - `Rotation(rotm[3][3])` — apply a 3×3 rotation matrix.
 * - `Matrix(trm[4][4], lr)` — left- or right-multiply by a 4×4 matrix.
 * - `Invert()` — replace the matrix with its inverse.
 * - `Reset()` — reset to the identity matrix.
 * - `IsIdentity()` — test whether the rotation part is identity (tol. 10⁻⁵).
 *
 * The `mIsMisaligned` flag is set by subclasses when a DB-misalignment
 * correction has been applied.
 */

/**
 * @class AgMLPosition
 * @brief Combined position/rotation record with DB-misalignment support.
 * @ingroup StarAgmlUtil
 *
 * Inherits `AgTransform` (4×4 matrix arithmetic) and `AgParameterList<double>`
 * (named parameter store with placement context).  Adds:
 * - `Misalign(tablename, row, options)` — multiplies the current matrix by a
 *   misalignment delta fetched via `AgMLDbFunctor`.  The `"invert"` option
 *   applies the inverse.
 * - `SetOrder(kGeneral|kRotTran|kTranRot)` — controls the composition order of
 *   rotations and translations.
 * - `GetX/Y/Z()` — retrieve translation components.
 * - `GetAngles(θx,φx,θy,φy,θz,φz)` — extract six G3 angles from the current
 *   rotation state.
 * - `Reference(…)` — reset and set rotation from G3 angles.
 * - `AlphaX/Y/Z(alpha)` — axis rotations delegating to `RotateX/Y/Z`.
 */

/**
 * @class AgMLDbFunctor
 * @brief Singleton functor interface for fetching misalignment matrices from the geometry DB.
 * @ingroup StarAgmlUtil
 *
 * The default implementation returns the identity matrix.  A real
 * DB-connected implementation (`AgMLDbMatrix`, declared in
 * `StarAgmlLib/AgPosition.h`) installs itself via `Register()` at program
 * start.  `lock()` / `unlock()` prevent or allow replacement of the
 * registered implementation.
 *
 * The functor signature is:
 * @code
 * void operator()(const char* tablename, const int row, double tr[4][4]);
 * @endcode
 */

/**
 * @}
 */
